# Restored-workspace rollout validation

The restored execution environment ran the graphics suite (8,976 checks), five Hox tests, four decimal-pattern tests, and existing puzzle/community checks (1,000 turns and 40 replays). 732 embedded JavaScript blocks parsed with Node; 44 SVG files parsed as XML. No browser/DOM/device/audio QA was available.

The main private SQLite database received nine foundations, three archetypes and 63 options. The imports ran twice, integrity_check returned ok, and all 19 original tables retained their row counts and content hashes. The same saved database identity was replaced with a new version.

Seventy current private HTML variants received the self-contained opt-in creative studio and new SVGs in the independent Elemental Workshop. Existing host content was verified recoverable exactly by removing the added creative block and reversing one optional visual-render statement. Host save keys were not edited. All 70 saved files were replaced preserving their identities and version histories. The saved distribution ZIP was rebuilt and replaced. A standalone studio and report were saved as additional deliverables.

The private Find the Star of Bethlehem Site published successfully at https://find-bethlehem-star.nathantabor.chatgpt.site with the same tool launcher. The source includes a /graphics-kit/ studio route. Forty-four Factory HTML source entry points receive this launcher in draft PR #17; the PR remains unmerged. No private builds, database records, source archives, or user media are committed to public Git.

The Redstone Site was not republished in this graphics rollout. The existing native Swift source bundle was not rebuilt or compiled. Production remote multiplayer, trained mentors, character rigs, and complete painted per-app art sets remain unfinished. Earlier availability statements in the historical drafts describe their state at creation; this report records the later rollout.
